The welcome tour's last page could run under «Start browsing»: the page
centres what it holds, so whatever was taller than the window spilled
below it, over the tour's button (the owner's window: the move-in note,
three tiles, «Get Claude for Mac» as a wide card, the Claude Code check).

- «Get Claude» shows only when no agent is there at all (none found, none
  in the check, Claude Desktop not just set up), once the check answered,
  and as the fourth tile of the same grid, not a wide card under it.
- The check's lines are as wide as the tiles.
- On a laptop-height window the mark, the headline and the gaps get
  smaller; a page still taller than the window scrolls under its own edge,
  never under the button.

Test: node --test chrome/browser/resources/webui_browser/meridian/layout_tests/onboarding_done.test.mjs
(real onboarding.css in headless Google Chrome, 800×600 to 2560×1440: no
overlaps, nothing under the button, one grid, no scrolling from 1024×640).
The layout tests share a small DevTools launcher, layout_tests/cdp.mjs.

